
~ title

The Beggar

=>


~ start

A dirty and dishelved beggar approches you, carying with him a small rucksack.
	He waves his hand around, and gestures to your gold pouch.
	[wait=1][br]He looks hopeful.

=> action


~ action

- Give 3 gold
	if Game.inventory.has(Items.GOLD, 3)
		do Game.inventory.remove(Items.GOLD, 3)
		%
			You give the beggar some gold, and he thanks you, with much gratitude and happiness, bidding you farewell.
		%
			He reveals himself as a [[wealthy|rich]] [[prince|aristocrat|merchant]], and in payment for your generosity pays you back thrice in return!
			do Game.inventory.add(Items.GOLD, 9)
	else
		You do not have enough gold.
		=> action

- Give 1 gold
	if Game.inventory.has(Items.GOLD, 1)
		do Game.inventory.remove(Items.GOLD, 1)
		%
			You give the beggar some gold, and he thanks you, with much gratitude and happiness, bidding you farewell.
		%
			He reveals himself as a [[rich]] [[aristocrat|merchant]], and in payment for your generosity pays you back twice in return!
			do Game.inventory.add(Items.GOLD, 3)
	else
		You do not have enough gold.
		=> action

- Ignore
	% The beggar becomes saddened, the hope bleeding away from his face, and he walks quietly away into the distance.
	%
		The beggar suddenly becomes enraged!
		#%
		He starts beating you, however you manage to repel him, but not in time to avoid some bruises.
		do Game.player.apply_stat(StatType.HEALTH, -5)
		#% He starts to grab at your belongings and runs off.

=> END